2. Remove Lore from Discover’s implementation

File: js/screens/discover-screen.js

Remove the following:

* The LORE_ENTRIES import from ../data/lore.js.
* The entire buildLorePage() function.
* The Lore section definition in the SECTIONS array.
* Any Lore-specific rendering or narrative scaffolding.
* Comments describing Lore as part of Discover.

Keep the existing generic reference-page helpers if Movement or Launch still uses them.

The final section registry must contain exactly:

* fighters — using buildFightersPage.
* movement — using buildMovementPage.
* launch — using buildLaunchPage.

Do not change how Fighters is initially selected.

Preserve the existing automatic activation system, ARIA tab relationships, roving tabindex, panel visibility, and keyboard/gamepad navigation.

Ensure no Lore panel or tab is constructed, registered, rendered, or focusable.

3. Delete the Lore data module

File: js/data/lore.js

Delete this file entirely.

The file currently defines LORE_ENTRIES, containing the editorial entries for the world and fighters.

Once Lore is removed, this registry serves no remaining purpose.

Do not leave an empty array, empty module, compatibility export, or unused replacement.

Verify that no active imports or runtime references to LORE_ENTRIES remain.

