6. Preserve Discover’s navigation and behavior

Removing Lore must not break the menu system.

The new navigation order is:

Wide screens (vertical rail)

Fighters → Movement → Launch

Narrow screens (horizontal rail)

Fighters → Movement → Launch

Verify the following behavior:

* Discover always opens on Fighters.
* Each section can be selected by mouse, touch, keyboard, and gamepad.
* Focusing a tab activates its section.
* Exactly one section is selected at a time.
* Hidden panels cannot receive focus.
* The selected tab uses the correct roving tabindex.
* Keyboard/gamepad movement skips no section and encounters no empty navigation position.
* Moving from a reference panel toward the rail returns focus to its active tab.
* Movement and Launch retain independent scrolling with gamepad support.
* Returning Home and reopening Discover resets to Fighters.
* The Fighters browser retains its previously browsed fighter according to existing behavior.

Preserve Back, Escape, Backspace, and controller Back behavior.

Do not modify shared navigation infrastructure unless strictly required.

7. Preserve all remaining Discover features

Fighters must remain fully functional.

Preserve:

* Read-only fighter roster.
* All playable and locked roster slots.
* Animated fighter previews.
* Shared 1–5 difficulty ratings.
* Localized play-style descriptions and modal dialog.
* Controller and keyboard navigation.
* Empty-roster and unrated-fighter states.
* Existing fighter ordering and selection behavior.

Movement must remain unchanged in content and mechanics.

Preserve its universal movement descriptions, registry-driven content, localization, formatting, and scrolling.

Launch must remain unchanged in content and mechanics.

Preserve Launch Point, Base Launch values, directional launches, the formula, and existing visual markers.

Do not modify any gameplay values, combat systems, fighter definitions, assets, or underlying movement/launch registries.

Lore removal must have zero gameplay impact.

